course: dictionary
lesson: 3363
title: Exciting words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Exciting is an adjective. It describes something that makes you feel very happy and eager, so much that you want to know what happens next. «Too much screen time can make you grumpy and sleep badly, because bright screens and exciting games keep your brain awake.» Here exciting games are full of action, so your brain stays busy when it should switch off.
explain: Look for clues around the word. «Clickbait is a scary or exciting title made to get clicks.» The clue is made to get clicks: a title that makes you want to click, because you feel eager to know more. Swap in your meaning, eager to know more, and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Exciting is part of the verb excite, which changes to excites, excited and exciting. Learning the family of words helps you spot them. Something can be exciting, or you can feel excited by it. Both come from the same idea of eagerness and action.
fact: Exciting means making you feel very happy and eager, wanting to know what happens next.
fact: Something exciting is new, fun or full of action.
fact: Exciting is an adjective, and it has more exciting and most exciting forms.
fact: The verb excite has the forms excites, excited and exciting.
fact: Slang: «lit» means exciting, and «grim» means horrible.
exercise: «Clickbait is a scary or exciting title made to get clicks.» In this sentence, what does exciting mean? | Hard to read | Old and dusty | Very quiet and calm | *Making you eager to know more
exercise: Which word is a form of the verb excite? | explore | exit | expert | *excited
exercise: «Bright screens and exciting games keep your brain awake.» What does this tell you about exciting games? | They are slow and boring | *They are full of action and keep your brain busy | They are only for grown-ups | They make you go to sleep at once
test: Which phrase means the news made people eager to hear more? | ancient news | *exciting news | barely news | glum news
test: Grim means horrible. Which word means the opposite feeling to exciting? | lit | fun | *grim | new
exam: Mia says, «I can't wait to see the ending, it's so exciting!» What does exciting mean here? | *Making her eager to know what happens next | Making her tired and sleepy | Making her ill | Making her quiet and still
